      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Biomass and biofuel technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biomass accounts for approximately 4.2% of global energy supply and about 60% of all renewable energy use globally as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/biomass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"First-generation biofuels are produced from food crops like corn and sugarcane, while second-generation biofuels use non-food biomass such as agricultural waste and wood\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/bioenergy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Bioethanol and biodiesel are the two most commercially developed biofuels, representing approximately 90% of global biofuel production\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewables-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced biofuels, including cellulosic ethanol and algae-based biofuels, are being developed to improve sustainability and reduce competition with food crops\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/bioenergy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biomass direct combustion for electricity and heat generation remains the largest biomass application, accounting for over 80% of biomass energy use\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewables-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Anaerobic digestion of organic waste produces biogas containing methane, which can be used for electricity, heat, or as a vehicle fuel\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/bioenergy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global biofuels market is projected to grow from approximately 142 billion liters in 2022 to over 200 billion liters by 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewables-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Sustainable feedstock sourcing and avoiding deforestation are critical challenges for biomass industry expansion to ensure carbon neutrality\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.fao.org/documents/card/en/c/CB9435EN/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
