      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Microgrid and distributed energy systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"A microgrid is a localized grouping of electricity sources and loads that normally operates connected to the main traditional grid, but can disconnect and function autonomously when needed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/microgrid-overview\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids can integrate renewable energy sources such as solar panels, wind turbines, and battery storage systems to increase energy resilience and reduce carbon emissions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/microgrids-101\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) include small-scale power generation units, energy storage systems, and controllable loads that are dispersed throughout the electrical network.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/news/program/2023/distributed-energy-resources.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global microgrid market was valued at approximately $28 billion in 2022 and is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate of 13.2% through 2030.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/microgrid-market\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids improve grid reliability by providing backup power during outages and can reduce peak demand charges through smart load management and energy storage optimization.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/73032.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced inverters and smart controls are critical components that enable microgrids to seamlessly transition between grid-connected and islanding modes while maintaining voltage and frequency stability.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/smart-inverters-overview\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Distributed energy systems can reduce transmission and distribution losses by generating electricity closer to consumption points, potentially improving overall system efficiency by 5-15%.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy16osti/65023.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Community microgrids serve multiple customers and can provide economic benefits through shared renewable generation, reduced energy costs, and improved power quality across neighborhoods.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/lpo/community-microgrids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
