      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar energy (photovoltaic and thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) solar panels convert sunlight directly into electricity using the photovoltaic effect, while solar thermal systems use the sun's heat for water heating or space heating applications.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/solar-photovoltaic-and-solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global solar PV capacity reached approximately 1,400 GW by 2023, with China leading production and installation of solar panels worldwide.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/news/solar-pv-global-capacity-sets-new-record\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar energy costs have declined by approximately 90% over the past decade, making it one of the cheapest electricity sources in many regions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2023-May/Renewable-Cost-Database\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Monocrystalline silicon PV cells currently achieve commercial efficiency rates of 20-22%, while laboratory prototypes have demonstrated efficiencies exceeding 47% using multi-junction cells.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems can achieve 50-80% thermal efficiency for water heating applications, compared to typical electric water heaters operating at 90-95% electrical efficiency.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/solar-water-heaters\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells represent an emerging technology with laboratory efficiencies reaching 33% and potential for low-cost manufacturing at scale.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/news/program-highlights/2023/nrel-perovskite-solar-cells.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar energy installations accounted for approximately 4.2% of global electricity generation in 2023, with projections to reach 20% by 2050 in net-zero scenarios.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/news/solar-pv-set-for-spectacular-growth\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors to concentrate sunlight and generate heat for electricity production, with some plants incorporating thermal storage to provide power after sunset.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/concentrating-solar-power\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
