      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Geothermal energy systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Geothermal energy provides baseload power with capacity factors typically between 70-90%, making it one of the most reliable renewable energy sources available.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy12osti/51604.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global geothermal electricity generation capacity was approximately 14 GW in 2020, with the highest production in countries like Iceland, New Zealand, and Indonesia.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021-Jun/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Enhanced Geothermal Systems (EGS) represent an emerging technology that can create economically viable geothermal resources in regions without natural geothermal reservoirs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy17osti/69351.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Direct-use geothermal applications (heating, cooling, and thermal processes) represent approximately 23% of total global geothermal energy consumption, with significant growth in heat pump technologies.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.thinkgeoenergy.com/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Geothermal systems have typical operational lifespans of 25-50+ years with relatively low operational and maintenance costs once installed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.eia.gov/energyexplained/geothermal/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) from geothermal plants ranges from $60-100 per MWh, competitive with other renewable sources when resource quality is favorable.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/analysis/data/cost_curves.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Induced seismicity from fluid injection in geothermal reservoirs can be managed through careful operational practices including microseismic monitoring.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-induced-seismicity\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Geothermal heat pumps for residential and commercial heating/cooling can reduce energy consumption by 30-70% compared to conventional systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/heat-pump-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
