      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Nuclear fusion and advanced nuclear technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The International Thermonuclear Experimental Reactor (ITER) in France is the world's largest fusion experiment, designed to demonstrate that fusion energy is scientifically and technologically feasible for commercial electricity production.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iter.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"In December 2022, the U.S. National Ignition Facility achieved fusion ignition, producing more energy output than was delivered to the fuel, marking the first time net energy gain from fusion was achieved in a controlled setting.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/national-ignition-facility-achieves-fusion-ignition\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Commonwealth Fusion Systems (CFS) is developing a compact fusion reactor called SPARC, with plans to demonstrate net energy gain and enable construction of commercial fusion power plants by the early 2030s.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.commonwealthfusion.com/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tokamak Energy and other private companies are pursuing alternative magnetic confinement designs and inertial confinement fusion approaches as pathways to commercial fusion power.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.tokamak.energy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced nuclear fission technologies including small modular reactors (SMRs) and fast breeder reactors are being developed to improve safety, reduce waste, and enable decentralized power generation.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/news-stories/small-modular-reactors-smrs\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Nuclear fusion produces no greenhouse gas emissions during operation and creates minimal long-lived radioactive waste compared to fission reactors.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.world-nuclear.org/information-library/current-and-future-generation/fusion-power.aspx\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China's EAST tokamak achieved a record fusion reaction temperature exceeding 120 million degrees Celsius in 2021, sustaining the reaction for extended periods.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.xinhuanet.com/english/2021-06/01/c_139975907.htm\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Challenges remaining for commercial fusion include achieving sustained net energy gain consistently, developing materials that can withstand extreme conditions, and scaling prototype reactors to commercial viability.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-022-03402-5\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
  "role": "assistant",
