      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy storage and battery systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lithium-ion batteries dominate the energy storage market, accounting for approximately 95% of global battery storage deployments as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global battery storage capacity reached approximately 14 GWh in 2022 and is projected to grow to over 4,000 GWh by 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solid-state batteries are emerging as a next-generation technology that could offer higher energy density and faster charging compared to conventional lithium-ion batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/news/program/2023/solid-state-battery-research.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Flow batteries, particularly vanadium redox batteries, are being deployed for long-duration energy storage applications (4-12 hours) in renewable energy systems\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/long-duration-storage-shot\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The cost of lithium-ion battery packs has declined by approximately 89% between 2010 and 2020, making energy storage increasingly economically viable\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/batteries-and-secure-energy-transition\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermal energy storage systems, including molten salt systems, can store heat for concentrated solar power (CSP) plants, enabling electricity generation at night\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/thermal-energy-storage.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped hydroelectric storage remains the largest form of energy storage globally, accounting for approximately 90% of the world's energy storage capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/hydropower\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Compressed air energy storage (CAES) systems can store energy by compressing air in underground caverns and releasing it through turbines when needed\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/compressed-air-energy-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Sodium-ion batteries are emerging as a lower-cost alternative to lithium-ion batteries, with commercial production beginning in 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/sodium-ion-batteries-set-for-faster-uptake\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The U.S. Department of Energy's Long Duration Storage Shot targets 90% cost reductions for energy storage systems lasting 10+ hours by 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/long-duration-storage-shot\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
