      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Floating solar and offshore wind integration\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Floating solar photovoltaic (PV) systems can be deployed on water bodies such as reservoirs, lakes, and ponds, reducing water evaporation by up to 70% while generating electricity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Dec/Floating-Solar-Photovoltaic-Systems-Technology-Potential-and-Challenges\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Offshore wind farms are typically located 5-15 km from the coast in shallow to moderate water depths (less than 50 meters for fixed foundations)\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/offshore-wind-outlook-2024\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Co-locating floating solar and offshore wind on the same platforms or nearby water areas can improve grid stability by combining complementary generation patterns and reducing overall marine space requirements\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00835-4\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Floating offshore wind turbines using tension-leg or spar buoy designs can operate in water depths exceeding 200 meters, enabling deployment in deeper waters\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy21osti/80736.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global floating solar capacity reached approximately 4 GW by 2023, with China accounting for over 60% of installations\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/data-and-statistics/data-tools/renewable-capacity-statistics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Floating solar panels operate at lower temperatures than rooftop systems due to water cooling effects, improving energy conversion efficiency by 5-15%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.solarpowerandchemicalenergy.com/floating-solar-panels.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Environmental considerations for floating solar and offshore wind integration include impacts on marine ecosystems, bird and bat migration, and navigation corridors\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iucn.org/resources/issues-briefs/offshore-renewable-energy-and-marine-conservation\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hybrid floating renewable energy platforms combining wind and solar technologies are being developed to maximize ocean space utilization and reduce total infrastructure costs\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261922006486\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
