      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Advanced materials for renewable energy\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved power conversion efficiencies exceeding 25% in laboratory settings, representing a major advancement over traditional silicon solar cells and offering potential for low-cost manufacturing\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00829-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Graphene and other two-dimensional materials exhibit exceptional electrical and thermal conductivity properties that enable enhanced performance in energy storage devices, photovoltaics, and supercapacitors\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360544222011568\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solid-state batteries utilizing ceramic electrolytes like yttria-stabilized zirconia (YSZ) demonstrate higher energy density and improved safety characteristics compared to conventional lithium-ion batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-00716-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced carbon materials including carbon nanotubes and carbon fiber composites are increasingly used in wind turbine blades to reduce weight while maintaining structural integrity, improving energy efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1369702121000432\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Halide double perovskites and tin-based perovskites are being developed as lead-free alternatives for photovoltaic applications to address toxicity concerns while maintaining photoconversion efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.chemrev.0c01229\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) demonstrate significant potential for hydrogen storage and carbon capture applications in renewable energy systems due to their high surface area and tunable pore structures\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0008622321000689\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"High-entropy alloys (HEAs) are emerging as promising catalytic materials for electrochemical energy conversion, including hydrogen evolution reaction and oxygen reduction reaction with improved durability and reduced precious metal requirements\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41578-021-00372-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermochromic and electrochromic smart window materials can dynamically control solar heat gain, reducing HVAC energy consumption in buildings by 15-30% when integrated into renewable energy systems\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038092X20300056\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
