      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Environmental impact assessment\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) is a systematic process for identifying and evaluating the potential environmental effects of proposed projects before implementation, including direct, indirect, and cumulative impacts\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.unep.org/explore-topics/environmental-assessment\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"EIA for renewable energy projects typically evaluates impacts on land use, water resources, biodiversity, air quality, noise, visual landscape, and socioeconomic factors\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/publications\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar photovoltaic installations have relatively low environmental impacts during operation but require assessment of land use conversion, habitat disruption during construction, and end-of-life panel disposal\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy12osti/54672.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind energy projects require EIA scrutiny for bird and bat mortality, noise generation, shadow flicker, electromagnetic interference, and visual landscape impacts\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.fws.gov/ecological-services/endangered-species-protection-implementation-associate\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydroelectric projects present significant environmental concerns including fish migration barriers, altered water flow regimes, reservoir flooding of terrestrial ecosystems, and greenhouse gas emissions from impounded water\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iucn.org/resources/issues-briefs/hydropower-and-dams\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Cumulative impact assessment is increasingly recognized as essential for evaluating multiple renewable energy projects and infrastructure simultaneously affecting ecosystems and communities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.unep.org/resources/report/environmental-impact-assessment-guidance-documents\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Geothermal energy development requires EIA for induced seismicity, groundwater contamination risks, and thermal impacts on surface water bodies\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-potential-environmental-impacts-geothermal-energy-development\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biomass and bioenergy projects require assessment of land use change, soil degradation, water consumption, and biodiversity impacts from feedstock production\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/bioenergy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
