      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors or lenses to concentrate sunlight onto a small area, converting solar energy into heat that drives turbines for electricity generation, unlike photovoltaic systems that convert light directly to electricity.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72022.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP systems can incorporate thermal energy storage (TES) systems, typically using molten salt, that allow plants to continue generating electricity after sunset, providing dispatchable power.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Jun/Renewable-Energy-Statistics-2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The major CSP technologies include parabolic troughs, solar towers/central receivers, linear Fresnel reflectors, and dish-Stirling systems, with parabolic troughs and solar towers being the most commercially developed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72022.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP plants require direct normal irradiance (DNI) and are most economically viable in regions with high and consistent solar radiation, such as arid and semi-arid areas between 15\u00b0-35\u00b0 latitude.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021/Jun/Renewable-power-generation-costs-in-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global CSP capacity has grown modestly, reaching approximately 6.3 GW by 2022, with Spain, the United States, and the Middle East being leading markets for deployment.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2023/Apr/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) has declined from approximately $380/MWh in 2010 to around $60-80/MWh by 2021, driven by technological improvements and economies of scale.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021/Jun/Renewable-power-generation-costs-in-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP plants require significant water resources for cooling systems, which can be a limiting factor in arid regions where most potential CSP sites are located.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy12osti/55625.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Parabolic trough systems, the most mature CSP technology, achieve thermal efficiencies of approximately 70-80% in converting sunlight to heat, with overall system efficiencies of 15-25% for electricity generation.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72022.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar tower technology (central receiver systems) can reach higher operating temperatures (600-900\u00b0C) compared to parabolic troughs (400\u00b0C), potentially enabling higher thermodynamic cycle efficiencies.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72022.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP hybrid systems combining solar generation with natural gas or biomass backup have been developed to provide stable baseload power and improve capacity factors.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2020/Apr/Renewable-Energy-Integration-in-Power-Grids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
